Rāma confers with Lakṣmaṇa and Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa --- Vibhīṣaṇa reports bird spies marked guards at every gate --- Vibhīṣaṇa counts elephants and chariots and crores of foes --- Rāma sends Nīla east and Aṅgada south --- Rāma sends Hanumān west and takes north himself --- Rāma posts Sugrīva and Jāmbavān and Vibhīṣaṇa centrally --- Rāma sets monkey shape as sign and advances